1.1.0
  - Refresh the series for the Linux 7.3 rebase upstream did (the base
    image moved to kernel 7.3.4). 0001, 0002, 0004, 0005 and 0006 are
    content-identical to the previously vendored revision (f05991ace64a);
    only their anchors moved.
  - 0003 rewritten upstream on top of KytyPS5-Native's bc250-amdgpu patch
    (faf53a5): bc250_flush_by_runlist is now a site bitmask (1 = unmap,
    2 = map) instead of a bool, and the runlist-rebuild flush covers the
    map-side and SVM map/unmap paths, not just the unmap ioctl. The
    map-side case is the one that actually faults (hipFree/hipMalloc VA
    reuse with stale translations).
  - 0008 (upstream 0028): KFD VMID GFX-hub flushes over the MMIO path
    0001 uses, instead of the KIQ, which stops answering under sustained
    multi-process compute. Hardware-tested upstream on a BC-250 (HIP
    stress: ~20 KIQ flush failures -> none).
  - 0009 (upstream 0029): amdgpu.bc250_cc_wgp_mask, per-shader-array WGP
    enable masks for boards with defective harvested WGPs, from
    ForceConstant's patch in upstream issue #14. Opt-in; an unset or
    unparsable mask leaves the registers as fused. Not booted upstream.

1.0.0
  - First release. The series is intentionally limited to patches that are
    inert outside a BC-250 or that fix a crash: the KFD TLB and compute
    idle paths, a TTM NULL guard, the kernel-side sclk range, the 40CU
    unlock as an opt-in module parameter, and a read-only marker.
